  "summary": "Party crews were organized groups of Latino teenagers that planned and hosted underground events, parties, and raves during the late-1990s and early-2000s in Los Angeles, California.",
  "description": "Party crews were organized groups of Latino teenagers that planned and hosted underground events, parties, and raves during the late-1990s and early-2000s in Los Angeles, California.\n\nMost are not nearly as prominent as they once were.\n\nMuch like Tagger crews, party crews or pc’s did not have a structure as many gangs of the time. They were often very problematic for police due to lack of infrastructure and leadership, in most cases making it uncontainable and difficult to identify potential members .",
